[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known as one issue. Its own table shows two causes, and the note under it a third problem the desk found: reports where the date moves by one day. Each needs its own ticket and its own fix.

<Callout>
Not known. Three problems, each with its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

- **parser** - the shared parser reads every date month first, and day-first tenants see months flipped. Tracked in [issue #1](https://github.com/wojciechbednarz/mega-s01e03-kb-clean/issues/1).
- **hint** - booking-v3's form prints MM/DD/YYYY under the date field, so day-first tenants type month first on purpose and the form reads it their way. A different bug, with a different fix. Tracked in [issue #2](https://github.com/wojciechbednarz/mega-s01e03-kb-clean/issues/2).
- **one-day move** - the note under the table: reports the desk read as a date moving by one day, not swapped (a time-zone fault). Filed under parser by tenant. Tracked in [issue #3](https://github.com/wojciechbednarz/mega-s01e03-kb-clean/issues/3).

Intake tagged many of these from the reporter's browser, and that tag is a guess: it is wrong for part of each group.

